    13	---
    14	
    15	# Backend
    16	
    17	FastAPI app defined in `backend/app/main.py`. Entry point: `app` (a `FastAPI` instance).
    18	
    19	## Responsibilities
    20	
    21	- Serves the REST API under `/api/v1` (see [routers](../routers/index.md)).
    22	- In production, also serves the built frontend as static files from `app/frontend`
    23	  (`app.frontend("/", directory=FRONTEND_DIR)`) — so the `backend` container is the
    24	  only one that needs to be reachable from outside Docker (see
    25	  [deployment/topology](../deployment/topology.md)).
    26	- Talks to [db](db.md) via SQLModel/SQLAlchemy, engine created in `app/core/db.py`.
    27	- Optionally reports errors to Sentry if `SENTRY_DSN` is set and `FASTAPI_ENV` is not
    28	  `"development"` (`app/main.py`).
    29	
    30	## Key files
    31	
    32	| File | Role |
    33	|---|---|
    34	| `app/main.py` | App instantiation, CORS, router + frontend mounting |
    35	| `app/api/main.py` | Aggregates routers into `api_router` |
    36	| `app/api/deps.py` | `SessionDep` (DB session), `CurrentUser`/`TokenDep` (auth) |
    37	| `app/core/config.py` | `Settings`, loaded from `../.env` |
    38	| `app/core/security.py` | Password hashing, JWT creation |
    39	| `app/models.py` | All SQLModel models |
    40	| `app/crud.py` | DB read/write helpers |
    41	
    42	## Generated client operation IDs
    43	
    44	`app/main.py` passes `generate_unique_id_function=custom_generate_unique_id` to the
    45	`FastAPI(...)` constructor, which returns `f"{route.tags[0]}-{route.name}"` (e.g.
    46	`items-read_items`) instead of FastAPI's default path/method-derived ID. This exists
    47	solely so the generated TypeScript client (see
    48	[regenerate-frontend-client](../../.agents/skills/regenerate-frontend-client/SKILL.md))
    49	ends up with short, readable method names (`ItemsService.readItems`) instead of
    50	verbose ones (`readItemsItemsGet`). Removing it changes every generated client method
    51	name.
    52	
    53	## Config
    54	
    55	Configured entirely through environment variables (`app/core/config.py`'s `Settings`,
    56	a `pydantic_settings.BaseSettings`), loaded from a `.env` file one directory above
    57	`backend/`. Required vars have no default and raise at startup if missing:
    58	`SECRET_KEY`, `PROJECT_NAME`, `DATABASE_URL`, `FIRST_SUPERUSER`,
    59	`FIRST_SUPERUSER_PASSWORD`.
